    "rationale": "TBX19 encodes TPIT, a T-box transcription factor restricted to pituitary POMC-expressing lineages and required for corticotroph differentiation and POMC/ACTH production. Recessive loss therefore causes low ACTH and cortisol with preservation of other pituitary hormones and a structurally normal pituitary. Strongest alternative resolved: MC2R-related familial glucocorticoid deficiency causes primary adrenal ACTH resistance, so ACTH is markedly elevated. This infant has low ACTH and cortisol with all other pituitary axes preserved, localizing the defect to TBX19-dependent corticotroph differentiation."
